            <section class="spread t-columns" id="economy"
             data-spread="economy"
             data-dimension="measures"><h2><span class="title"><span class="fb" lang="en">economy</span></span></h2><div class="prose-slot" lang="en"><p>Nairobi is home to the <a href="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2384385">Nairobi Securities Exchange</a> (NSE), one of Africa's largest <a href="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q11691">stock exchanges</a>. The NSE was officially recognised as an overseas stock exchange by the <a href="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q171240">London Stock Exchange</a> in 1953. The exchange is Africa's fourth largest in terms of trading volumes, and fifth largest in terms of Market Capitalization as a percentage of GDP.</p><a class="read" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nairobi#Economy">Economy ↗</a></div><dl class="sheet" data-slot="sheet"><div class="row r-value"><dt><span class="fb-group"><span class="fb"
      lang="en">economy of topic</span><a class="add-label"
           href="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Special:SetLabel/gu/P8744"
           aria-label="Add a label in your language">+</a></span></dt>
<dd><span class="fb-group"><a href="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q106020188"><span class="fb" lang="en">economy of Nairobi</span></a><a class="add-label"
           href="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Special:SetLabel/gu/Q106020188"
           aria-label="Add a label in your language">+</a></span></dd>
<span class="tools">
        <span class="prov-none" title="—"></span>
        <a class="edit"
       href="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3870#P8744"
